  "s2instr2": {
   "id": "s2instr2",
   "page": 14,
   "kind": "instruction",
   "tab": "Step 2",
   "overline": "Step 2 · before Exercise 5",
   "title": "The resources an actor holds",
   "lead": null,
   "blocks": [
    {
     "h": [
      "Power, and why this step records resources instead"
     ]
    },
    {
     "p": [
      {
       "b": [
        "Power"
       ]
      },
      " here is an actor's capacity to affect what the system does: what gets decided, what reaches the agenda, and what goes unquestioned. That capacity is hard to judge directly and easy to guess at. What can be recorded instead is concrete: the ",
      {
       "b": [
        "resources"
       ]
      },
      " an actor holds that others in the system need. Recording the resources is this step's work; judging what kind of power they add up to comes later, once there is something to judge it against."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": [
      "The seven resources"
     ]
    },
    {
     "p": [
      "Seven kinds, enough to sort by and few enough to remember."
     ]
    },
    {
     "table": {
      "head": [
       [
        "Resource"
       ],
       [
        "What it means"
       ]
      ],
      "rows": [
       [
        [
         {
          "b": [
           "Formal authority"
          ]
         }
        ],
        [
         "Can decide, or change a rule"
        ]
       ],
       [
        [
         {
          "b": [
           "Money"
          ]
         }
        ],
        [
         "Holds or can redirect the funding"
        ]
       ],
       [
        [
         {
          "b": [
           "Delivery capacity"
          ]
         }
        ],
        [
         "Does the work on the ground"
        ]
       ],
       [
        [
         {
          "b": [
           "Information and expertise"
          ]
         }
        ],
        [
         "Knows something the others need to know"
        ]
       ],
       [
        [
         {
          "b": [
           "Access"
          ]
         }
        ],
        [
         "Can get to whoever decides"
        ]
       ],
       [
        [
         {
          "b": [
           "Legitimacy"
          ]
         }
        ],
        [
         "Can credibly speak for others"
        ]
       ],
       [
        [
         {
          "b": [
           "Public attention"
          ]
         }
        ],
        [
         "Can make an issue visible, or keep it quiet"
        ]
       ]
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "h": [
      "Two rules while you fill the table"
     ]
    },
    {
     "list": [
      [
       "An actor that seems to need two layers is usually two actors, as a ministry's policy directorate and its inspectorate are two actors with different reach."
      ],
      [
       "An affected group that splits into halves wanting different things is two actors. A single entry that hides the split will not survive the rest of the analysis."
      ]
     ],
     "ordered": true
    },
    {
     "h": [
      "A third rule, about who gets left out"
     ]
    },
    {
     "p": [
      "Include those the system acts on, not only those who act. Name the group by its position in the system (\"households refused on income grounds since 2023\")."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": [
      "The four columns before the resources"
     ]
    },
    {
     "p": [
      "Columns ",
      {
       "b": [
        "1"
       ]
      },
      " to ",
      {
       "b": [
        "4"
       ]
      },
      " are the four admission tests from page ",
      {
       "ref": "s2instr1"
      },
      ": ",
      {
       "b": [
        "1"
       ]
      },
      " affects the problem, ",
      {
       "b": [
        "2"
       ]
      },
      " is affected by what the system produces, ",
      {
       "b": [
        "3"
       ]
      },
      " holds something others need, ",
      {
       "b": [
        "4"
       ]
      },
      " can start or stop a change. Tick every one that applies. An actor with no tick in any of the four does not belong in the table, and column ",
      {
       "b": [
        "2"
       ]
      },
      " is the one to read back: if nothing is ticked down that column, the list has only the actors who act, and not those the system acts on."
     ]
    },
    {
     "opposite": [
      "Opposite: Exercise 5. Turn the book sideways."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
